        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Harry Craft\n- Places: Ellisville, Mississippi; Jones County, Mississippi\n- Organizations: Cincinnati Reds; Major League Baseball\n\nFacts:\n- Harry Craft was born on April 19, 1915, in Ellisville, Mississippi.\n- Harry Craft was an American Major League Baseball player and manager.\n- Harry Craft was a center fielder for the Cincinnati Reds from 1937 to 1942.\n- Ellisville is a city in Jones County, Mississippi, and it was the first county seat of Jones County.\n- Harry Craft died on August 3, 1995.\n- Ellisville had a population of 4,448 in the 2010 census.",
